export anchor ConsultingStyle:
    number: 186
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Consulting
    idea: A formal partner's briefing on warm paper, with a serif voice, a burgundy accent, numbered sections and exhibits, all held to one narrow reading column.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #fbfaf7, the page and the hollow last week dots
        white: #ffffff, fields and the bell button
        ink: #1e1b18, text, the table head rule and the 2px rule that opens each exhibit
        stoneInk: #5b544c, labels, meta, nav, axis and last week dot outlines
        rule: #d9d3ca, row hairlines and chart gridlines
        burgundy: #7a1f33, the primary button, the finding rule, section numbers, the current nav, this week dots and focus
        burgundyTint: #f4e9eb, the focused row fill
        onTrack: #2f6b3a, On track with a filled circle
        atRisk: #8a5a00, At risk with a half filled diamond
        behind: #9b2c1f, Behind with a crossed square
    type:
        Two stacks. Headings and figures use Iowan Old Style, Palatino
        Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif at 600. Body uses
        system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting is
        40px serif at 1.15, section heads 24px serif, the finding 20px
        serif, figures 40px serif, project names 16px serif, body 15px sans
        at 1.6, exhibit labels and nav 12px sans caps tracked 0.12 to
        0.14em.
    layout:
        A masthead up to 1080px wide has a serif Brightwork wordmark with a
        burgundy outlined square mark at left and at right an underlined
        search field, a square burgundy New project button, a square bell
        and the words Signed in as Mara Okafor. Below a hairline the six
        nav links sit centred in small spaced caps, Home burgundy and
        underlined. Everything after is one centred 760px column like a
        printed memo. A burgundy caps kicker Portfolio briefing sits over
        Welcome, Mara in large serif and the date in serif italic, then a
        pull line with a 3px burgundy left rule reading Principal finding.
        4 tasks are overdue and require attention. Four numbered sections
        follow, each with a small burgundy number beside a serif heading.
        Section 1 Summary is Exhibit 1, four large serif figures in a row
        split by vertical hairlines with labels under them, the overdue
        figure burgundy. Section 2 Projects has a one sentence lead, then
        Exhibit 2, a formal table of Project with team below, Complete,
        Tasks as 18 of 25, Due and Status, with an italic note that
        explains the status symbols. Section 3 Throughput has a lead
        sentence and Exhibit 3, a dumbbell chart with one row per weekday
        joining a hollow last week dot to a filled burgundy this week dot,
        each row labelled like 12 then 15, over a 0 to 20 axis. Section 4
        Recent activity is a list with the time in a narrow left column and
        the entry at right with item names in serif italic, ended by a
        centred row of three burgundy dots. Below 640px the figures go two
        by two, the table turns into stacked blocks with inline labels, the
        activity time moves above each entry and the chart scrolls
        sideways.
    spacing: An 8px unit. A 760px column, 36px between sections, 48px above the title, 12px table cells.
    density: Medium. One column of prose, figures and tables read top to bottom.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders: Hairlines between rows, a 2px ink rule opening each exhibit, a 1px ink rule under table heads and a 3px burgundy rule on the finding.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Very few. Thin 1.4 stroke line icons for search and the bell only.
        Status uses 12px geometric marks with the word, a filled circle, a
        half filled diamond and a crossed square.
    focus: A 2px burgundy outline offset 3px. A focused row also takes the burgundy tint fill.
    tone: Formal and measured, in full sentences, such as Principal finding and Six engagements are active.
